## Verification

```powershell
python verify.py
```

The verifier first checks the complete local packet-hash graph, including the
schema-specific G3U source binding, before it executes any theorem gate. A
stale dependency lock therefore fails at preflight rather than appearing later
as a mathematical regression. `.gitattributes` fixes repository text files to
LF so these byte-level locks remain stable across Windows, WSL and Linux
checkouts.

The target-Macaulay rank route uses WSL/Linux native exact engines. Its build
entry point discovers either a system LinBox/Givaro installation or the staged
`~/.local/opt/linbox-*/root/usr` layout. A nonstandard installation can be
selected with `MTT_LINBOX_PREFIX`; missing headers or runtime libraries fail
closed.

```powershell
python build_ust_f1016_native_tools.py
python assemble_ust_g3ap_selected_cayley_target_macaulay_rank_subcampaign.py --dry-run
python run_ust_g3ap_through_g3aq_closure.py --assemble-rank-subcampaign
```

The last command is valid only after the dry run reports at least 39,725
complete rows and all still-running exporters have been stopped, so no parent
process can overwrite the assembled campaign during certification.

The deeper K3 elimination takes about one minute on the reference machine and
is run separately:

```powershell
python verify_ust_g3f_q79_no_splitting_line.py --prime 5
```

Passing this verifier certifies only that the research contract is internally
consistent and locked to declared upstream evidence. It does not certify the
source hypothesis.
